{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore. Men of mockery.</b> Those who mock, saying that the words of HaShem are like 'command upon command.'" "<b>The rulers.</b> Some say it is from the root of ממשלה, and the meaning is 'princes,' but the correct view is that it is as in 'therefore the rulers say' (Numbers 21:27)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:34.801331207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}